{
  "slug": "revit-bim",
  "name": "Revit Bim",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Connect Claude to Autodesk Revit and Dynamo. Generate ready-to-run Dynamo Python scripts, query model data, detect clashes, audit model health, manage parameters, create schedules, export IFC, and save .dyn files — all from plain language. Includes 12 skills covering the full BIM workflow.\n\nCreated by Manas Bhatia (Architect and Design Technologist)",
  "longDescription": "Ships **25 skills**, **3 agents** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (25): `acc-api-setup` (Set up Python authentication and a reusable client for the Autodesk Platform Services (APS) API to access Autodesk…), `acc-coordinate` (Work with Autodesk Construction Cloud (ACC) Coordinate — list and inspect model sets, retrieve clash results, create clash…), `acc-design-collaboration` (Guide Revit ↔ ACC Design Collaboration workflows — setting up cloud worksharing, creating and consuming design packages, shared…), `acc-docs` (Manage Autodesk Construction Cloud (ACC) Docs — list folders and files, upload documents, download files, create folder structures,…), `acc-reports` (Export ACC project data to CSV or Excel — issues, RFIs, document logs, clash summaries, transmittals, and project…), `analyze-rooms` (Analyze rooms, spaces, and areas in a Revit model — GIA calculations, space program comparison, department breakdowns, unbounded/unplaced…), `audit-model` (Audit and analyze Revit model health, quality, and BIM standards compliance), `batch-rename-elements` (Batch rename Revit elements across any category using prefixes, suffixes, numbering sequences, or parameter-driven naming rules), and 17 more\n- **Agents** (3): `acc-agent` (Expert Autodesk Construction Cloud (ACC) specialist), `bim-agent` (Expert BIM Manager and Revit specialist), `project-setup-agent` (Expert Revit project configurator and BIM standards specialist)\n- **Hooks** (2): `PostToolUse`, `PreToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install revit-bim@claude-community` from `Utopia5327/revit-bim`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
